{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GeomSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.geometric_tail_bound_abstract","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.geometric_tail_bound_abstract","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.lean#L56-L75","doc":"Conditional theorem: under the uniform-bound conjecture, the\ngeometric-tail bound holds.\n\nFor a substrate parameter `q` with `0 < ℏ_q² < 1`, the tail\nof the brane-tower mass series after the first `N` terms is\nbounded by `delta_max · ℏ_q^{2(N+1)} / (1 - ℏ_q²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQSq","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.lean#L53-L54","doc":"The substrate Planck constant squared, instantiated abstractly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.uniform_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.uniform_bound","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The uniform-bound hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.delta_max_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.delta_max_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Non-negativity of the bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.delta_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.delta_max","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The asserted uniform bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.delta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.delta","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The per-level binding contribution at level `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.mk","kind":"ctor","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JetTowerUniformDeltaMax","kind":"class","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JetTowerUniformDeltaMax.lean#L34-L51","doc":"The conjecture, encoded as a class.\n\nA `JetTowerUniformDeltaMax ρ` instance asserts the existence\nof a finite real `delta_max` bounding the per-level binding\ncontributions `delta n` for all `n ≥ 1`. The unproved input\nis the existence of the instance; downstream conditional\ntheorems (geometric-tail truncation bounds) are then fully\nverified parametrically. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:jet-tower-uniform-delta-max","label":"conj:jet-tower-uniform-delta-max","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jet-tower-uniform-delta-max.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}